            <title>[LU-21270] sanity test_65k: setstripe 0 should succeed</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21270</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Marc Vef &amp;lt;mvef@whamcloud.com&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/c2bf4000-8dce-43f8-947e-dc376efa31e6" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/c2bf4000-8dce-43f8-947e-dc376efa31e6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_65k failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;setstripe 0 should succeed
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.59.74&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/134108" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/134108&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 5.14.0-687.39.1.el9_8.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Server&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.59.74&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/134108" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/134108&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 5.14.0-687.39.1.el9_8_lustre.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Intermittent: the setstripe -i 0 -c 1 inside the deactivated-OSC loop fails while one MDT OSC is deactivated and its max_create_count is 0. Here it follows "mkdir: cannot create directory d65k.sanity: Input/output error" and force_sync "Transport endpoint is not connected" on OST0000-osc-MDT0000.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not caused by the patch under test (69659 PS4, osc encryption folio locking): sanity was the only failed suite and test_65k the only failed subtest. It also shows up as a victim in master and master-next rolling-upgrade-mds runs, where the filesystem goes read-only. maloo test-history: 5 failures in 30 days on lustre-master, lustre-master-next and lustre-reviews.&lt;/p&gt;



&lt;p&gt;VVVVVVV DO NOT REMOVE LINES BELOW, Added by Maloo for auto-association VVVVVVV&lt;br/&gt;
sanity test_65k - setstripe 0 should succeed&lt;/p&gt;</description>
